From: Rockpod iPod 6G Android qualification work
Subject: [PATCH] arm: s5l8702: add storage-free N25 RAM diagnostic target

This target is intentionally narrower than a normal board port. It qualifies
volatile execution on the iPod Classic before persistent storage work. The
board runs Rockbox's proven iPod 6G cold DRAM sequence from IRAM, verifies both
32 MiB banks without touching storage, and then exposes only RAM-backed USB
DFU. There is no ATA, CE-ATA, MMC, NAND, SPI flash, filesystem, partition, or
persistent environment support.

The N25 identity, 64 MiB DRAM geometry, ARM926EJ-S CPU, UART pins, clock gates,
and memory-controller values come from the Rockbox ipod6g target. The ROM's
CPU/AHB/APB clocks are retained; only OSC0 selection, the 12 MHz MIU refresh
clock, and Rockbox's two SDRAM gates are changed before the cold-start sequence.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/s5l8702-n25-ramdiag.dts b/arch/arm/dts/s5l8702-n25-ramdiag.dts
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..945c87bd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/s5l8702-n25-ramdiag.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+ OR MIT
+/*
+ * Apple iPod classic (6th generation), N25.
+ * Volatile RAM diagnostic profile: persistent storage is not described.
+ */
+
+/dts-v1/;
+
+#include "s5l8702.dtsi"
+#include "s5l87xx-nxx.dtsi"
+
+/ {
+	compatible = "apple,n25", "samsung,s5l8702", "apple,arm-platform";
+	model = "Apple iPod classic (6th generation) RAM diagnostic";
+	rockpod,safety-profile = "ram-only-no-storage";
+};
+
+&memory {
+	reg = <0x08000000 0x04000000>; /* 64 MiB SDRAM */
+};
+
+&clkref {
+	clock-frequency = <12000000>;
+};
+
+/* No ATA, CE-ATA, MMC, NAND, NOR, or filesystem node is permitted here. */
